{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","title":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2651,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","line":4471,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Constant Signature]\n\\label{def:pseudo-metric-has-signature}\n\n\\uses{def:pseudo-metric-signature-at}\n\n\n\n\nA pseudo-Riemannian metric $g$ \\emph{has signature $(r,s)$} if its signature is\n$(r,s)$ at every point. A pseudo-Riemannian manifold of signature $(r,s)$ is a\npair $(M,g)$ with this property.\n\\end{definition}\n\nOn an $n$-manifold, a constant signature satisfies $r+s=n$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Constant Signature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a70736575646f2d6d65747269632d6861732d7369676e6174757265\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apseudo-metric-signature-at\">↗ def:pseudo-metric-signature-at</a> <p></p>A pseudo-Riemannian metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span> <em>has signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s)$\">$(r,s)$</span></em> if its signature is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s)$\">$(r,s)$</span> at every point. A pseudo-Riemannian manifold of signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s)$\">$(r,s)$</span> is a pair <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> with this property.  <p></p>On an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold, a constant signature satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r+s=n$\">$r+s=n$</span>.","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-metric-signature-sum","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:gram-schmidt-bilin","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","title":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","label":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:lorentz-metric","title":"def:lorentz-metric","label":"def:lorentz-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-signature-at-a-point","title":"prop:hypersurface-signature-at-a-point","label":"prop:hypersurface-signature-at-a-point"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-signature","title":"prop:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-signature","label":"prop:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-signature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-submanifold","title":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-submanifold","label":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-hypersurface-submanifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","title":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","label":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:product-pseudo-riemannian","title":"exer:product-pseudo-riemannian","label":"exer:product-pseudo-riemannian"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","title":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Constant Signature]\n\\label{def:pseudo-metric-has-signature}\n\n\\uses{def:pseudo-metric-signature-at}\n\n\n\n\nA pseudo-Riemannian metric $g$ \\emph{has signature $(r,s)$} if its signature is\n$(r,s)$ at every point. A pseudo-Riemannian manifold of signature $(r,s)$ is a\npair $(M,g)$ with this property.\n\\end{definition}\n\nOn an $n$-manifold, a constant signature satisfies $r+s=n$.","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","title":"def:pseudo-metric-signature-at","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}